00:23:02:230 [12604] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R78] MVEC TRANSPORT f=3901 mode=3 REAL | producer: copies=3841 missing=61 size-rejected=0 lock-skipped=0, arm held 239 frame(s) | consumer: seals seen valid=3840 invalid=60 contract mismatches=0 flag disagreements=9 | region 2560x1440 fmt=34 pitch=10240 bytes=14745600 at slot offset 29491712 of 44237312 | GPU 1: unpacked=3836 bound=2892 skipped=60, scale=(1.000, 1.000). 98.5% of sealed frames carried vectors. COPIES IS THE ONE TO WATCH: it counts frames where the bind hook fired and a copy was recorded. If it stays at zero the probe published a handle nobody binds, and MVec never reaches the model whatever the rest of this line says. SKIPPED IS NOT AN ERROR - it counts frames with no vectors, which is what a menu looks like, and those frames are handed NONE rather than the last frame's motion.
00:23:02:232 [12604] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R87] MVEC FRAME ALIGNMENT f=3901 | evaluates=2952 | elapsed 1=2008 2=940 3=3 4=1 5=0 6=0 7=0 8+=0 | worst=4 | 68.02% at 1. A motion vector describes ONE game frame; NR reprojects by whatever it is handed. When the frame NR blends against is older than one, history lands SHORT by this factor - zero error at rest, growing with speed, and no constant MVecScale can fix it. The scale is multiplied by this per evaluate. IF THIS LINE IS FLAT AT 1 AND THE ARTEFACT IS UNCHANGED, PACING IS ELIMINATED and what remains is units or sign. P4.1's skipped-frame counter predicts about 99.5% at 1, so a materially lower figure here is a desync no counter has shown us.
